{
    "file": "High_Performance_Sales_Teams_Indoor_and_Outdoor.docx",
    "title": "High Performance Sales Teams: Indoor & Outdoor",
    "duration": "5 Days",
    "overview": [
        "High-performing sales teams combine a clear commercial strategy, effective leadership, disciplined sales processes, strong customer relationships, and consistent execution. Indoor sales teams and outdoor field sales teams face different operating conditions, yet both must convert opportunities into profitable business while delivering a reliable customer experience.",
        "This five-day course equips sales managers, supervisors, and team leaders with practical methods to build and manage high-performance indoor and outdoor sales teams. Participants examine sales planning, territory and account coverage, lead management, pipeline discipline, team structures, recruitment, onboarding, coaching, motivation, performance metrics, field productivity, inside-sales effectiveness, and cross-channel coordination.",
        "Through sales cases, KPI exercises, territory-planning workshops, call and visit simulations, coaching practice, team-performance diagnosis, and action planning, participants develop the skills to strengthen sales productivity, accountability, collaboration, and sustainable results."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Sales managers, regional and area sales managers, indoor sales supervisors, field sales supervisors, team leaders, business-development managers, sales operations professionals, key account managers, and professionals responsible for managing, coaching, or coordinating inside and outside sales teams."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "Interactive presentations, commercial performance case studies, sales-process mapping, team and territory design workshops, KPI and pipeline analysis, customer-call and field-visit role plays, coaching simulations, incentive-design discussions, forecasting exercises, collaborative planning, and practical action-plan development."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Sales team leadership",
        "Indoor and outdoor sales management",
        "Sales planning and target setting",
        "Territory and account management",
        "Sales pipeline management",
        "Performance coaching",
        "Sales forecasting",
        "Sales productivity analysis",
        "Team motivation and engagement",
        "Customer relationship management",
        "Sales process improvement",
        "Cross-functional coordination"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Distinguish the operating requirements of indoor and outdoor sales teams and design appropriate coordination mechanisms.",
        "Translate commercial goals into team, territory, and individual sales plans.",
        "Define roles, coverage models, customer segments, and sales responsibilities.",
        "Use KPIs to monitor activity quality, conversion, revenue, margin, and customer outcomes.",
        "Build disciplined prospecting, opportunity qualification, and pipeline-review routines.",
        "Improve field-visit planning, route productivity, and inside-sales call effectiveness.",
        "Recruit, onboard, coach, and develop salespeople against observable standards.",
        "Deliver constructive performance feedback and address underperformance consistently.",
        "Use realistic forecasting and sales data to guide managerial decisions.",
        "Motivate teams with fair recognition, incentives, and a supportive performance culture.",
        "Improve handoffs between indoor, outdoor, service, and sales operations teams.",
        "Develop a measurable improvement plan for a high-performance sales team."
    ],
